# Live gallery / popup mocks — never text-only options

Hard rule for diana’s dashboard (`/Users/diana/my-dashboard`).

## Trigger phrases (any of these)

**show me**, **mock up** / **mock-up** / **mockups**, **options**, **which one**, **placements**, **alternatives**, **design choices**, or any ask to *see* UI/layout variants before picking.

## Required delivery

1. **Open a real visual mock** she can look at — not a chat bullet list.
2. Prefer:
   - dedicated `{feature}-mocks.html` / `{page}-mocks.html` on the dashboard, **or**
   - a full-screen dismissible overlay / popup on the live page (`?mock=…` / `#mock-…`)
3. Serve at `http://127.0.0.1:8080/` (or whatever `serve.py` is using) and **give her the URL**.
4. Prefer **one composition**: options side-by-side or tabbed in a single popup/page — not scattered chat screenshots.
5. Match real chrome feel (collage, pills, tools) when mocking UI — not empty wireframe boxes alone.
6. After she picks, wire the winner to the live board.

## Never

- End with “Say which one and I’ll wire it” / “Which do you prefer?” **without** the visual mock already open
- Reply with A/B/C/D as a **text-only** multiple-choice in chat
- Rely on inline chat images alone when a live gallery/popup is feasible
- Ask her to imagine the placement from prose

## Pattern references

- `accomplishments-mocks.html`, `capture-panel-mocks.html`, `margin-mocks.html`
- `depth-placement-mock.html` (overview depth A–D placements)

## Naming

- `{page}-mocks.html` — background / full-page direction
- `{feature}-mocks.html` or `{feature}-mock.html` — UI chrome / panel / placement
